<section>
  <h2>Setting up Tempo Adjust in Safari</h2>
  <p>
    Safari extensions are off until you turn them on, and Tempo Adjust also
    needs permission to run on Bandcamp and Discogs. If the tempo controls
    don't appear, work through the steps for your device.
  </p>

  <h3>iPhone and iPad</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Open the <strong>Settings</strong> app and go to
      <strong>Apps &gt; Safari &gt; Extensions</strong>. On iOS 17 it's
      <strong>Safari &gt; Extensions</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Tempo Adjust</strong> and turn it on.</li>
    <li>
      On the same screen, tap <strong>Extension Settings</strong>. Tempo
      Adjust's setup page opens in Safari.
    </li>
    <li>
      Tap <strong>Allow</strong>, then <strong>Always Allow</strong>, so Tempo
      Adjust can run on bandcamp.com and discogs.com.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    If you don't see Extension Settings, open Safari, tap the extensions menu
    in the address bar, then tap Tempo Adjust.
  </p>

  <h3>Mac</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Open Safari and go to <strong>Safari &gt; Settings &gt; Extensions</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>Check the box next to <strong>Tempo Adjust</strong>.</li>
    <li>
      Tempo Adjust's setup page opens in Safari. Click <strong>Allow</strong>,
      then <strong>Always Allow</strong>, so it can run on bandcamp.com and
      discogs.com.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    If the setup page doesn't appear, click the Tempo Adjust icon in Safari's
    toolbar.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <h3>The controls don't show up on a page</h3>
  <p>
    Tempo Adjust adds controls next to the player on Bandcamp album, track,
    wishlist, and collection pages, and next to the videos on Discogs release
    pages. Other pages on those sites don't have a player, so nothing is
    added. If a page does have a player and the controls are missing, reload
    the page once.
  </p>
  <p>
    If they still don't appear, the extension probably doesn't have access to
    the site yet. On Chrome and Firefox, click the Tempo Adjust icon in your
    browser's extensions menu. Its settings page opens and, if any access is
    missing, shows an <strong>Allow</strong> button. Click it and reload the
    page. In Safari, work through the setup steps above.
  </p>

  <h3>Why doesn't BPM detection work on Discogs?</h3>
  <p>
    Discogs plays music through embedded YouTube videos, and the extension
    can't read audio from those. BPM detection is only available on Bandcamp.
    The tempo slider works on both sites.
  </p>

  <h3>The tempo slider sounds glitchy</h3>
  <p>
    The slider changes the speed of the page's own player. Some browsers
    briefly stutter while the rate changes, especially in Safari. Letting go of
    the slider applies the new tempo cleanly.
  </p>

  <h3>Where is the purchase export?</h3>
  <p>
    Log in to Bandcamp, click your profile picture in the top right corner,
    and choose <strong>purchases</strong> from the menu. Tempo Adjust adds a
    summary of your spending and an export button at the top of that page. It
    only works on your own purchases page, since that's the only place
    Bandcamp lists them.
  </p>

  <h3>What do tips and donations unlock?</h3>
  <p>
    Nothing. Tips in the Safari app and donations from the Chrome and Firefox
    extensions are optional, and every feature is available without one. They
    only help keep the project going.
  </p>

  <h3>
    I installed Bandcamp Tempo Adjust on Chrome or Firefox, but I'm not seeing
    Tempo Adjust on Discogs
  </h3>
  <p>
    On Chrome and Firefox, Tempo Adjust is two separate extensions, one for
    each site. Bandcamp Tempo Adjust only runs on Bandcamp, and Discogs Tempo
    Adjust only runs on Discogs. Install the other one from the
    <a href="/tempo-adjust/#install">Tempo Adjust page</a>. The Safari app
    covers both sites on its own.
  </p>
</section>

